or":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-03-31T15:12:26Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T12:12:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.3 (stable) and 4.4.1 (stable)\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Godot v4.4.1 stable - Vulkan (Forward+) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 Super\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf window is resized to a size with uneven width or height (e.g. 1013x611) when ```display/window/stretch/mode``` is Disabled and ```display/window/stretch/aspect``` is Expand, several visual bugs appear: some random (?) letters inside Labels have 1 pixel offset, also some sections of Sprite2D are scaled (they shouldn't). One enabled Camera2D **must** be present.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a project.\n2. Go to project setting and set ```display/window/stretch/mode``` to Disabled and ```display/window/stretch/aspect``` to Expand.\n3. Create a scene, add label with some text and Camera2D (enabled) into it.\n4. Run the game and resize the window to an uneven width or height.\n5. Look at the label.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[github-uneven-window-size-bug-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19537384/github-uneven-window-size-bug-mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104848/reactions","total_count":0,"